Complete local PHP example; the app itself does not execute it:
```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
class Task { public function run(): void {} }
$method = (new ReflectionClass(Task::class))->getMethod('run');
echo $method->isPublic() ? 'public' : 'not public', "\n";
```

Optional local transfer task: Inspect getNumberOfParameters on a known method without invoking user-selected code. You may trace it without a PHP interpreter; reading completion is not proof of a local run.

getNumberOfParameters takes a reflected method as receiver and returns its declared parameter count, including optional parameters. It does not invoke the method. This known local method has one parameter.
```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
class Task { public function run(string $topic): void {} }
$method = (new ReflectionClass(Task::class))->getMethod('run');
echo $method->getNumberOfParameters(), "\n";
```
Expected output: 1.

